\f1\fs22 The popularity of the Elvi drew no official attention from \cb3 the Directorate of Moral Observance for a very long time\cb1 . Conformity to the laws of business and adherence to the social hierarchy, ensured the distribution of wealth always flowed upward and the shit always flowed down. Respect was only permitted to look up and was always to be returned with scorn. \
At first glance, the Elvi served this purpose very well. Considered as only one entity and unable to claim individual royalties or accumulate sufficient wealth to wield any individual power, they were ripe for exploitation. Deprivation of economic advancement was usually sufficient to crush any fanciful dreams of social climbing and even if there were one hundred thousand of them jitter-bugging around the Dominion, no Elvis would wield power.\
Fans of the Elvi, \cb3 the Dawks\cb1 , saw themselves as a benign, loosely affiliated group of wildly enthusiastic music fans that, for the most part, did not really care about social change, the environment or some dude that might get born in the future. About the only seditious act they indulged in was pasting 
\f2\i \cb3 \'93The one-after-the-one is coming\'94
\f1\i0 \cb1  posters on any and every vertical surface that would readily accept glue. A few appeared on walls here and there, but before long, the posters became ubiquitous. \cb3 The Pale was transformed into a thicket of papier-m\'e2ch\'e9 monoliths\cb1 , gathered together in praise of The Dawkins and silently awaiting the one-after-the-one. Where most saw a collection of useless, drug fucked stoners, the \cb3 Moral Compliance Directorate \cb1 saw the Dawks representing doctrinal divergence of the worst kind, an organised threat to the natural order. \
The Elvi managed to fly under the radar of Moral Compliance until they spoke of the \'93One after the One\'94, the great leader to come, as the deliverer of hope. Moral Compliance cared not about silly songs righteously regaling the merits of saving trees and whales. \cb3 There were fuck-all trees and no whales left to save anyway. They could sing all they liked, it would amount to nothing. Prophesy was not something the company gave much credence, but the Elvi were preaching social change, equality and freedom. Giving hope to working class scum was something that would not be tolerated, the lows would not be permitted to taste of such rich fruit. The minority of the opulent must be protected from the majority. Radical and decisive action was needed to ensure they dined on ashes forever.\

